Apple CEO <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tim-cook/">Tim Cook</a> today pledged that the company will make a donation toward relief and rebuilding work in Nepal and Tibet, where flash floods and mudslides have killed hundreds of people.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2022/07/Apple-Park-View.jpeg" alt="" width="1440" height="790" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-854420" /><br/>
On Wednesday, part of a Himalayan glacier collapsed, briefly damming a river before a surge of water and mud hit communities downstream. Many people are dead or missing, and roads, bridges, and homes near the Nepal–Tibet border have been destroyed.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><blockquote class="twitter-tweet"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">Our thoughts are with all those affected by the tragic flash floods and mudslides in Nepal and Tibet. Apple is making a donation to support relief and rebuilding efforts on the ground.</p>&mdash; Tim Cook (@tim_cook) <a href="https://x.com/tim_cook/status/2093170528643412092?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">August 28, 2026</a></blockquote> <script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script></div><br/>
<br/>
This marks Apple's fifth disaster relief pledge in just over two months, after the company supported <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/18/apple-donating-to-indonesia-earthquake-relief/">Indonesia's earthquake recovery</a> earlier this month and previously stepped in for crises in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/26/apple-donating-to-venezuela-earthquake-relief/">Venezuela</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/30/apple-donating-to-european-wildfire-relief-efforts/">Southern Europe</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/30/apple-japan-earthquake-donation/">Japan</a>. <br/>
<br/>
